# The addons a client shell carries: one repository per line, as addons.lock names it, `#` comments.
#
# Read by tools/shell_lock.sh, which the shell export (tools/server.in: shell_lock_begin, shell_left_out_addons) and
# tools/check_shell_addons.sh use. Only these go into a shell build and its addons.lock; every other addons.lock line
# is for servers only, and its addon reaches a player as a dot-cloud overlay pack (DotCloudAddonSet).
#
# OWNER RULE: no game addon here, ever. fc-weapons, zee-dot-weapons, zed-dot-weapons, natural-disasters and anything else one
# game brings stay out of the shell: baked in, fc-weapons took the web pck from 44 MB to 147 MB, and a shell that carries a
# game's addon pins every game to that build's copy. tools/check_shell_addons.sh fails when this list names anything but a
# dot-* addon, or when addons.lock names a dot-* addon this list does not (add it here when the shell should carry it).
dot-2d
dot-achievements
dot-audio
dot-auth
dot-bot
dot-bot-record
dot-browser
dot-chat
dot-cloud
dot-combat
dot-console
dot-core
dot-economy
dot-effects
dot-entity
dot-flashlight
dot-friends
dot-fx
dot-game
dot-inventory
dot-leaderboard
dot-lighting
dot-loadout
dot-locale
dot-log
dot-map
dot-match
dot-matchmaking
dot-menu
dot-mobile
dot-moderation
dot-net
dot-npc
dot-npc-ai
dot-npc-ai-director
dot-objective
dot-party
dot-peer-to-peer
dot-physics
dot-platform
dot-player
dot-player-char
dot-player-class
dot-player-controller
dot-procedural-generation
dot-profile
dot-profiler
dot-props
dot-radio
dot-replay
dot-server
dot-server-query
dot-server-security
dot-settings
dot-sim
dot-spawn
dot-spectate
dot-sql
dot-stats
dot-team
dot-timer
dot-trail
dot-ui
dot-user
dot-user-avatar
dot-vehicle
dot-voice
dot-vote
dot-weapon
dot-weather
dot-workbench
